{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Final tidy of the inquiry's own pointers, now that the last two variants are settled by source. The parent investigation's discriminator no longer names the peer-side and trim-side variants as open: the peer-side behaviour is settled by the handler reading (a peer compacts to a forwarded index only when that index is within its own decided index, and otherwise try_snapshot refuses it with UndecidedIndex while handle_compaction discards the error, so the peer keeps its state instead of mirroring the leader's loss), and the trim-side variant is settled by the per-node initialisation of the recorded accepted vector, which keeps the trim bound at or below a truthful replica's own accepted index. What could still change the judgment there is therefore another execution, not another reading: a compaction requested with local_only = false and sampled on the peers, or a lagging replica re-synchronized after a trim rather than after a snapshot. The trim child's discriminator was reworded to the same effect, recording that its gap is answered for every route it named - the in-cluster re-synchronization executed and silent, the truthful-peer route closed by source, the storage-level reads executed and aborting under overflow checks - with the single remaining way to move it being a build without those checks or another implementation of the Storage trait. No account, knowledge entry, gap or execution changed; this closes the run with every question carrying a current account, its own receipts and controls, and an accurate statement of what, if anything, would still move it.\"}"}}
